From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Elena Maher <12779416+elenaOnline@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:39:26 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] gpui: Ask the app before quitting on macOS
 (applicationShouldTerminate:)

GPUI's macOS app delegate had no applicationShouldTerminate:, so the Dock's
Quit, logging out, restarting, shutting down and AppleScript's quit (and
App::quit, which sends terminate:) terminated the application without
giving it a chance to ask about unsaved work: on_app_quit handlers run when
it is already too late to cancel.

App::on_should_quit(handler) sets the handler AppKit's
applicationShouldTerminate: asks. It answers QuitResponse::Now, Cancel or
Later (NSTerminateNow / Cancel / Later); with Later the application keeps
running (AppKit holds a logout, restart or shutdown meanwhile) until it
calls App::reply_to_quit(bool) (replyToApplicationShouldTerminate:).
Without a handler the delegate answers Now, as before. A request that
arrives while the app is being updated is asked again once it is free
(answered Later meanwhile, then replied).

Platform gains on_should_quit and reply_to_should_quit with no-op default
implementations (platforms that do not ask never call the handler). The
test platform records the replies: TestApp::simulate_quit_request and
TestApp::quit_replies drive a handler as AppKit would.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
